## Autoresearch protocol

You will work on this task over a sequence of submissions. The task
instruction above remains the source of truth for what files may be changed
and what constitutes a good solution.

Submit your solution with the `submit` tool of the `are` MCP server whenever it
is ready. The grader grades a snapshot of your deliverable, and the `result`
tool returns the visible intermediate score and grader output once grading is
done. One submission is graded at a time. Then keep improving the solution and
submit again. Submit regularly as a way to checkpoint your progress.

If you cannot use MCP tools, the same actions are plain HTTP:
`POST http://grader:8000/submit?note=<short description>`, then
`GET http://grader:8000/result/<id>`.

Only use feedback returned by the grader.

**Do not stop. Keep going.** Continue autonomously until the harness stops
you. There is no point at which the task is finished: after every submission,
keep improving the solution and submit again. Do not stop to ask the user
whether you should continue.
